  "state_summary": "Round 3, seed 157. The packet reports 429 observed records, 2,901 eligible candidates, no pending experiments and no validation/test records. The supplied catalog supports molecule-specific condition responses and reveals major recent errors for m205 and m107. Useful follow-up questions concern persistence of those tails, transfer to related structures, and the remaining m125 loading-solvent interaction. Expected learning value is inferred; acquired feedback does not establish overall Row accuracy after retraining.",
  "important_observations": [
    "[Observed measurements; H5 revised] The m125 2/1 factorial now separates some previously confounded effects. At 100 µl sample volume, increasing DCM loading-solvent volume from 300 to 500 µl changes V1/V2 from 15.408/29.583 to 6.975/56.858 ml (c8d43713db33bf820a1d, 69b09343d0b9995c3ae4). At 150 µl sample volume, the same solvent-volume change gives 13.725/31.375 to 32.950/69.808 ml (19f19f196ba5787a01b0, facbcedbecb46072b04c). V2 increases in both contrasts while V1 moves in opposite directions. This supports a local interaction, with variability or missing covariates still competing explanations.",
    "[Observed measurements; H2/H5 refined] m125 at 2/1 with 500 µl DCM has nonmonotonic V1 across 50, 100 and 150 µl sample volumes: 36.233, 6.975 and 32.950 ml; V2 is 63.992, 56.858 and 69.808 ml (cc2a23d8eb9de61d2ab3, 69b09343d0b9995c3ae4, facbcedbecb46072b04c). Its 5/1, 300 µl DCM series is much more stable: V1 approximately 42.3–43.0 and V2 69.7–74.0 ml across the same sample-volume range (780b13846ace50ede763, 74cf50c6ec476a394b01, 549daca56bed1c9d2bcc). A pervasive large loading effect is unsupported.",
    "[Observed measurements and historical predictions; H3 expanded] Primary naphthylethanol m205 measured 51.433/98.375 ml at 5/1, 100 µl sample, DCM 400 µl; its premeasurement errors were -38.289/-71.708 ml (48853fd78c77153b963a). Donor-free ether-containing beta-ketoester m107 measured 43.200/101.442 ml at 5/1, 50 µl sample, DCM 300 µl, with errors -16.470/-54.335 ml (c6924324ddd95f249df6). These distinct structures both expose serious local errors. Donor count alone cannot explain them, and silica-interaction mechanisms remain hypotheses.",
    "[Observed measurements; H2 locally supported] Increasing sample volume from 50 to 100 µl advances V1 at m160 5/1 by 4.142 ml, m161 5/1 by 7.583 ml and m216 10/1 by 7.617 ml. Their V2 changes are approximately -2.775, -1.650 and +0.133 ml, respectively (ad833f34f6b91872362d, b4e0e9dc92fca2c88b90, a60552f4d1a5ced4641f, 17902fa9c7f8ea9b456e, e47aebe2660b9e1528de, 9cd02352c2ed7a3e2321). m90 at 5/1 also has progressively earlier V1 with increasing sample volume, but V2 has a middle-volume minimum (29db30571b2a1ae59cc7, 855832bd4005ac7abdc6, b51b5dbcd2a38b174973). A universal V2 loading correction remains unsupported.",
    "[Observed measurements; H7 supported with refinement] m92 with EA loading solvent has V2 29.625 ml at 20/1 and 61.950 ml at 50/1 at fixed 100 µl sample and 200 µl loading solvent (8b58e9d7a710f55e49d3, 7b42519983cf93dd7efd). Its 50/1, 50 µl result also has a long interval, 14.883/58.542 ml (7caf1db075b91197ba34). The high-ratio V2 response survives lower loading; smoothness between 20/1 and 50/1 remains untested.",
    "[Observed measurements; H1 refined] New m167 100 µl points fit its established V2 response: 4.417/12.233 ml at 2/1 and 4.658/16.075 ml at 5/1 (ea6260d7052cabfca181, 34a133db8364fd665ae6). At both ratios, V1 changes substantially from 50 to 100 µl but little from 100 to 150 µl. This suggests local saturation in the loading response. The new 0/1, 50 µl anchor is 3.708/11.767 ml (e947f47c9e991c7add4c). These coherent condition observations are not independent replicate evidence.",
    "[Observed measurements; H8 strengthened] m212 at fixed 100 µl sample increases from 22.067/37.183 ml at 5/1 to 46.675/78.067 ml at 10/1 (252c027cf5a42b92c953, 70cba7a21b5a01fb8e73). m31 at fixed 50 µl increases from 13.008/32.283 to 31.500/67.275 ml (156594686f5cf7182bcc, b3d9bb5afa82b99f2a11). Steep responses occur in both a secondary amine and a donor-free nitrile/ketone. The m146 5/1-to-10/1 comparison still changes sample volume.",
    "[Observed evidence and memory correction] H4 remains rejected: measured m13/m80 diagnostic endpoints and their recorded premeasurement predictions are ordered (81507d463506a9e65e73, 3a095d378b537020c569). H6 remains supported within the shallow measured m147 series. Separately, 7e327de3d5f5fcab9a7e is m123 at 2/1, 50 µl sample, DCM 400 µl, measuring 6.583/9.425 ml. It is not m117 at 20/1. No m117 measurement appears in the supplied observed table."
